# Questions Bee Box is trying to address

{% questions %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How do we let people center their own focus?** Interactivity is a demand: what can we do without interactivity?

- Drop in information, thoughts, followups — interactivity only for failure
- Embrace high latency and asynchronicity

[Interaction model](https://beebox.run/docs/design/interaction-model.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**Does every action require a poke?** Can proactivity remove another interaction? Can it stay under control and easy to understand?

- Notifications: the best and worst of this
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**What is good design for chat?** Can we *design* chat, not just treat it as a given? What should responses look like? Are we going to let behavioral signals replace design?
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**What are the categories of conversation?** How do we let the user say more than the AI? Listen, comment?

- Modes: converse, narrate, listen, comment
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**If the agent doesn't always *respond*, then how else does it *react*?** Record, structure. Respond visually? Initiate mode switches? Interject?
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How can we let the agent help with the *entire* app?**

- Everything is a document/file, including UI
- Let the agent see what you see

[Extensibility](https://beebox.run/docs/design/extensibility.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How do you trust the agent's decisions?** How do we monitor *why* things happen, not just *what* happened?

- Bureaucracy: make the agent fill out paperwork, before and after

[Trust](https://beebox.run/docs/design/trust.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How do you create the decision criteria?** How do you turn intuition into documented criteria? How do we use corrections to fix not just the mistake, but future mistakes?
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
We have an agent. It does things for you. How do we track it? Not just how do we know what it did — but **how does the agent itself understand what it did?** What is its sense of history and process?

- Git as history
- Git as explanation (commit messages)
- The agent as explainer
- Not meant for the user to interact with Git, or even Git history

[How it works](https://beebox.run/docs/07-how-it-works.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
The chat log is how we understand what the agent understands. It's a document it's responding to as much as a log. But **how does it model you?** How does it know where your focus is, what you're reacting to?

- It can see your screen
- Card activity: scrolled, explored, modified
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How do we preserve authenticity of voice?** How do we keep the AI from rewriting, paraphrasing, and confusing its own output for original instructions?

- Quotation markup, core to everything it writes
- No paraphrasing as a primary rule

[Provenance](https://beebox.run/docs/capabilities/provenance.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**So how can it draw those authentic words out of you?** You don't want it to create them — but to give you the support that keeps you from having a blank page.
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How will the information accumulate without ending up with chaos?** How does it stay consistent? Queryable, repairable?

- Typed cards: plain files with strict schemas
- Always room for overflow information

[Shape it later](https://beebox.run/docs/capabilities/shape-it-later.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How do we share new ways to do things?** How do we give people both custom experiences and best practice in how things are built up?

- Best-practice documents, consensus approaches, shareable tools and ideas instead of plugins
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**What happens when there's multiple channels of improvement — you're improving your system, and upstream is improving it too?**

- That's both very hard and suddenly kind of doable, because the agent just goes in and fixes everything
- Migrations carried by the agent

[Migrations](https://beebox.run/docs/dev/migrations.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How do you give the agent power over its environment without letting it break everything, including itself?**
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How does one space hold different parts of your life, when they overlap and yet they kind of don't?**

- Everything accessible, focused areas
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How does this engage with our understanding of space, not just language?** Space is one of our really strong intellectual capabilities — and that's kind of about how to build this as a home.
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How do we make the compute cost reasonable for the user?**

- Built on the coding-agent subscription
- …which is useful for a lot more than the box

[What it requires](https://beebox.run/docs/08-what-it-requires.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**When the subscription doesn't cover everything, how do you pay for all the little things?** How do you support little APIs, login providers, AI services, API keys?
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**What can we create without a dependency on capital?** How big a thing can we make without funding? And without it just being a fake it till you make it until the funding comes in.

- If code is cheap, then let's make use of that
- 100% agentically coded
- One person, low capital (but one person isn't enough)

[Agent coding](https://beebox.run/docs/dev/agent-coding.html)
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How do we remove the principal agent problem?** How do we align the software with the user?

- Principal agent problem: does the software work for the user, or for the software provider?
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How does it create a space that feels like yours?** Not a space you control or that you own, but that feels like home. A lot of our software feels like a hotel. It has all the trappings of a home. It's very well kept, but it's never where you belong personally.

- A home is messy, in progress
- You bring everything home before you sort it all out
- It's familiar
{% /question %}
{% /questions %}

Bee Box is meant to become what you want it to be. To be moldable into something that's uniquely yours.

## Cut from the talk

{% questions %}
{% question state="open" %}
**And how do you handle the boundaries — external data, where the craziness is just the nature of it?**
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**How do you give the agent tools that fit over all the things you do, so it's not having to invent new things to do normal behaviors?**

- bbx: one composable command line
- Direction as its own layer
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**How do we make all the statefulness happen in a unified way?** Committing something was to do it — actions become nouns. I don't think it's been successful.
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**You know that it's no worse than the agent you're using.** It's every bit as smart as Claude, or whatever back end you have.
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**What kind of reactivity?** How do we codify it — programmatically sometimes, non-programmatically other times — without being expensive? Because starting with an agent is expensive.
{% /question %}
{% question state="answered" %}
**So many places where you might use a static schema, I use code.** We put live things into the system instead of dead things.
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**Addictive apps drive you through the same loop continuously.** What we want is for it to be driving you into new loops.
{% /question %}
{% question state="open" %}
**Can you have private spaces within a shared space?** How do you keep it from leaking? When everything's easier to do, leaking is easier too.
{% /question %}
{% /questions %}
